BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lasithi-agios-nikolaos-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-patron-of-agios-nikol-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271207
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Nikolaos\, patron of Agios Nikolaos town
LOCATION:Agios Nikolaos\, Crete (Lasithi)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The town named after the saint keeps 6 December as its patronal feast: vespers on the 5th\, hierarchical liturgy and a procession of the icon through the centre and along the lake on the 6th\, with the municipal band and school parades\, and the town's Christmas lights switched on around the same days. The tiny 8th-century chapel of Agios Nikolaos at the Minos Beach headland\, which gave the town its name\, also holds a liturgy.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#agios-nikolaos-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-patron-of-agios-nikol
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#agios-nikolaos-feast-of-agios-nikolaos-patron-of-agios-nikol
END:VEVENT
